@title EPISODE 20 • THE ENVELOPE
@bg penthouse_night
@show paris
Everything is good. That's what scares London.
Paris and Jayden are trying again, slowly. Suki and Jamal are talking. Alana keeps "accidentally" texting Cam. Priya calls London her "training partner" now, like it's a title.
@show cassie
Then Cassie shows up at the penthouse door at midnight, not smiling for once.
Cassie: I'm not here to start anything. I swear on my edges.
London: Then why are you here?
Cassie: Because my mom works in your dad's office. And I saw this.
She holds up a photo on her phone. An envelope on Frank Sterling's desk. "D. Williams" written on it. And a check.
Cassie: Your dad's been paying him, London. Since Family Weekend.
> [Bitchy] "Get out, Cassie. You're lying. Again." -> e1
> [Bold] Call Diggy. Right now. -> e2
> [Good] Call your father first. -> e3
> [Sweet] "...Why are you telling me this?" -> e4
*e1
@add Cassie_Threat 1
Cassie: (at the elevator) Ask him. If I'm lying, I'll leave the team. That's how sure I am.
The doors close. London doesn't sleep.
@jump end
*e2
@add Diggy_Trust -1
It rings. And rings. Voicemail. "Yo, it's Diggy, leave it at the beep." London hangs up before the beep.
@jump end
*e3
@add Parent_Trust 1
Frank: (after a long silence) Baby... it's not what you think. Come home this weekend. We'll talk in person.
That is the least comforting sentence London has ever heard.
@jump end
*e4
@add Cassie_Friendship 2
Cassie: (quiet) 'Cause I know what it's like to find out last. Everybody always tells me last.
*end
@hide
@bg penthouse_window_night
London stands at the window. The whole valley glittering. Somewhere out there, Diggy's asleep — or isn't.
Her phone buzzes. "D: can we talk tomorrow? there's something i should've told you."
End of Episode 20. To be continued...
